+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Deleting a product currently leaves carts and orders dependent on a live catalog row, so historical commerce data becomes unreadable and carts can no longer be recalculated or checked out. Product deletion must remove only the active catalog item while preserving cart safety and the immutable product snapshot required by order history.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Remove deleted products from carts when carts are read or recalculated, recomputing quantity, subtotal, and total from remaining products.
+- Reject attempts to add a deleted product with HTTP 404.
+- Preserve the purchased SKU, name, quantity, price, subtotal, and order totals after product deletion.
+- Keep merchant/customer order reads, order listing, status changes, and checkout functional after deletion.
+- Return HTTP 404 from the v2 product lookup for deleted products, without affecting other products.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `deleted-product-references`: Keeps carts safe and order history stable when catalog products are deleted.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+Affected catalog deletion and lookup services, shopping-cart retrieval/mutation and checkout flows, order persistence/population, and v1/v2 integration tests across `sm-core`, `sm-shop`, and their model modules. No new external dependency is required.
